{
  "stage": "write",
  "item": "ch04.s12",
  "inputs_hash": "3f6f98fa1c32ea77bf6df896e854874542be8a289ac7810f9550459fb9512bd0",
  "output_hash": "98e30817d748a27e0afb21fe7772f6cf23ccde37f05a239bf7289a1fb8808b48",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch04.s12",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.01",
            "text": "How should a GPT model turn its next-token scores into an actual token ID, and why is the choice of decoding rule so important for the text it produces?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.02",
            "text": "A simple decoding strategy selects the generated token with the largest probability score among all tokens in the vocabulary.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@66",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@70",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@72",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@75",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@77"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.03",
            "text": "To predict the next token in this strategy, the model output is examined for the index with the maximum probability score, and that token is chosen as the next token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@83",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@86",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@88",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@90"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.04",
            "text": "Choosing the next token this way is deterministic.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@120",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@123",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@185",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@193",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@223",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@224"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.05",
            "text": "That determinism motivates a probabilistic alternative.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.06",
            "text": "Instead of choosing the maximum-probability token, the logit tensor can be passed through softmax to obtain probabilities, and then the next token can be sampled with a multinomial distribution.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@133",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@139",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@142",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@150",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@153"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.07",
            "text": "Multinomial sampling selects the next token proportionally to its probability score.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@169",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@172",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@175",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@177"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.08",
            "text": "As a result, the token with the largest probability is still favored, but other tokens can also sometimes be selected according to their probabilities.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@197",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@199",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@200",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@202",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@204",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@206",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@211",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@215",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@217",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@219"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p01.09",
            "text": "This probabilistic choice enables more creativity in the model output and helps control randomness.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@227",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@229",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@232",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@235"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.01",
            "text": "Sampling becomes more useful once the logits are adjusted before softmax.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.02",
            "text": "Temperature scaling divides the logits by a temperature value and then applies softmax.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@237",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@238",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@240",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@243"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.03",
            "text": "When the temperature is increased, the next-token probabilities become more uniform, whereas a very low temperature produces a sharper distribution that favors one token more selectively.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@245",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@247",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@249",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@251",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@253",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@256",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@257",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@259"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.04",
            "text": "An animation is used to show this change from a sharp distribution at low temperature to a more uniform distribution at high temperature.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@266",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@268",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@270",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@273",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@274",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@276",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@277",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@280"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.05",
            "text": "Higher temperature values therefore lead to more uniformly distributed next-token probabilities and more diverse outputs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@465",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@467",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@469",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@471",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@473"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.06",
            "text": "This can explore less likely but potentially more interesting and creative paths, but it can also lead to grammatically incorrect or completely nonsensical output.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@475",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@478",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@480",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@482",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@485",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@486"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.07",
            "text": "A temperature that is too low gives a sharper distribution, while a temperature that is too high can produce nonsensical output.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1120",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1122",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1124",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1126",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1128"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p02.08",
            "text": "The weakness of temperature scaling by itself is that all tokens remain possible next tokens, including completely random ones.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@317",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@320",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@323",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@325",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@327",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@329",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@331"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.01",
            "text": "Top-k sampling fixes that specific problem by restricting which tokens can be considered at all.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.02",
            "text": "Top-k sampling keeps only the top k most likely tokens and excludes all other tokens from consideration.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@343",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@345",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@347",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@357",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@361",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@364"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.03",
            "text": "The filtering is done before softmax by keeping only the top k logits and replacing all other logits with negative infinity.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@373",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@375",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@377",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@379",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@399",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@401",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@403",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@404"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.04",
            "text": "When the non-top-k logits are replaced with negative infinity, softmax makes their probabilities effectively zero, so only the surviving top-k tokens can be selected.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@407",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@409",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@411",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@414",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@415",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@421"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.05",
            "text": "This removes tokens that do not make sense from the next-token candidates.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@423",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@425",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@427",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@429",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@432",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@434"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.06",
            "text": "In PyTorch, \"torch.topk\" applied to the next-token logits returns both the top k values and the indices where they occur.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@543",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@546",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@549",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@552",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@555",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@557",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@559",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@562",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@568",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@570"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p03.07",
            "text": "The code then uses \"torch.where\" to replace logits below the smallest top-k logit with negative infinity, and after softmax only the top-k tokens retain nonzero probabilities that sum to one.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@611",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@617",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@622",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@624",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@627",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@630",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@635",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@637",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@640",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@642",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@644",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@647",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@648",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@650",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@653"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.01",
            "text": "Once top-k filtering is in place, it can be combined with temperature scaling and probabilistic sampling into a single decoding workflow.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.02",
            "text": "The combined procedure is to obtain the logits from the model, keep only the top-k logits, replace the others with negative infinity, divide by temperature, apply softmax, and sample from the multinomial distribution.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@742",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@745",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@747",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@749",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@754",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@758",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@761",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@762",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@765",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@769",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@774",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@777",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@779",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1314",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1317",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1321",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1324",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1327",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1328",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1330",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1332",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1334",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1336"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.03",
            "text": "After top-k filtering and temperature scaling, multinomial sampling still favors the highest-probability surviving token most often, but the other surviving tokens can also be sampled according to their probabilities.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@709",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@710",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@713",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@717",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@719",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@721",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@723",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@725",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@727",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@728",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@730",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@732"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.04",
            "text": "This combination preserves some creativity through temperature scaling, blocks random tokens through top-k filtering, and makes token selection probabilistic rather than deterministic through multinomial sampling.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@787",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@791",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@793",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@795",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@797",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@799",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@801",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@804",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@806",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@807",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@809"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.05",
            "text": "Top-k sampling is used specifically because it addresses the temperature-scaling problem in which random low-probability tokens can still become the next token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1281",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1284",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1286",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1289",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1291"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p04.06",
            "text": "Restricting sampling to only the top k most likely tokens improves the meaning of generated tokens and helps avoid nonsensical or random output.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1294",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1297",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1299",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1300",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1303",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1305",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1307"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.01",
            "text": "The final generation function packages this decoding logic into the token-generation loop.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.02",
            "text": "A final function is written to generate the next token by combining temperature scaling and top-k sampling.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@813",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@815",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@817",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@819",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@866",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@868"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.03",
            "text": "This function takes the GPT model, the maximum number of new tokens, the context size, the temperature value, the top-k value, and an end-of-sample ID as inputs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@870",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@875",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@876",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@879",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@883",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@885"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.04",
            "text": "Inside the function, logits are obtained from the GPT output and then top-k filtering is applied, keeping only the top-k values in the logit tensor and replacing the rest with negative infinity.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@893",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@895",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@898",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@899",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@901",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@908",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@912",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@914",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@916",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@917"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.05",
            "text": "If the temperature is greater than zero, the logits are scaled by temperature, passed through softmax, and the next token ID is sampled from the resulting multinomial distribution.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@921",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@924",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@929",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@932",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@934",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@936",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@938",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@940",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@942",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@945",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@947",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@949"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.06",
            "text": "If the temperature is not specified, the next token is chosen by taking the token ID with the maximum probability instead of sampling.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@953",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@956",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@959",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@962",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@966",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@968",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@970",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@972"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.07",
            "text": "\"EOS\" stands for end of sequence.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@985",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@987",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@989"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.08",
            "text": "If an end-of-sequence token is encountered, generation can stop early; otherwise each new token ID is appended to the current IDs until the maximum number of new tokens is reached.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@989",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@993",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@997",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1000",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1003",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1007",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1010",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1013",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1016"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.09",
            "text": "The flow that is shown is: start from the logit tensor, apply top-k sampling, scale with temperature, sample the next token from a multinomial distribution, or use argmax if temperature is not specified, and keep appending tokens until the new-token limit is reached.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1018",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1020",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1023",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1025",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1027",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1029",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1031",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1033",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1036",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1038",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1040",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1043",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1046",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1048"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p05.10",
            "text": "The \"generate\" function now in use implements this token-generation process.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1050",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1052",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1054"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s12.p06",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p06.01",
            "text": "A concrete example shows how these choices change the produced text.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s12.p06.02",
            "text": "The new \"generate\" function is called with the GPT model, the input token IDs for \"every effort moves you\", a maximum of 15 new tokens, top-k set to 25, and temperature set to 1.4.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1085",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1087",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1091",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1094",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1096",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1099",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1100",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1103",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1117",
              "EhU32O7DkA4@1120"
            ]
          },
          {
